# A shell script with CRLF line endings fails on Linux with a "bad interpreter"
# error that names the right file and explains nothing. install.sh is fetched
# straight from this repository and piped into sh, so its endings must not
# depend on the autocrlf setting of whichever machine committed it.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are read by tools, not by Windows editors.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
